(- Superkey: K -> R, meaning K+ contains all attributes of relation R.) Tj
/F1 10.2 Tf
1 0 0 1 66.0 402.0 Tm
(- Candidate key: a minimal superkey. Remove any attribute from K, and it should no longer determine all) Tj
/F1 10.2 Tf
1 0 0 1 66.0 389.0 Tm
(  attributes.) Tj
/F1 10.2 Tf
1 0 0 1 66.0 376.0 Tm
(- Prime attribute: an attribute contained in at least one candidate key.) Tj
