0 0 0 rg
/F1 10.2 Tf
1 0 0 1 66.0 255.0 Tm
(- 1NF: values are atomic; no repeating groups or multi-valued cells.) Tj
/F1 10.2 Tf
1 0 0 1 66.0 242.0 Tm
(- 2NF: 1NF plus no partial dependency of a non-key attribute on part of a composite key.) Tj
/F1 10.2 Tf
1 0 0 1 66.0 229.0 Tm
(- 3NF: for every non-trivial alpha -> beta in F+, either alpha is a superkey, or each attribute in beta -) Tj
/F1 10.2 Tf
1 0 0 1 66.0 216.0 Tm
(  alpha is prime.) Tj
/F1 10.2 Tf
1 0 0 1 66.0 203.0 Tm
(- BCNF: for every non-trivial alpha -> beta in F+, alpha must be a superkey. BCNF is stricter than 3NF.) Tj
/F1 10.2 Tf
1 0 0 1 66.0 190.0 Tm
(- If a relation is in BCNF, it is in 3NF. A relation can be in 3NF but not BCNF when the dependent attribute) Tj
/F1 10.2 Tf
1 0 0 1 66.0 177.0 Tm
(  is prime.) Tj
